1
00:00:00,900 --> 00:00:04,566
Welcome to Module 5: Practice Fusion and Billing.

2
00:00:09,800 --> 00:00:13,221
Each month, after documenting the care plan in ThoroughCare,

3
00:00:13,271 --> 00:00:17,598
you submit the patient's encounter for billing, in Practice Fusion.

4
00:00:17,867 --> 00:00:20,158
You'll create this month's encounter.

5
00:00:20,433 --> 00:00:22,167
Add the care plan note.

6
00:00:22,433 --> 00:00:25,150
Attach the care plan file, and check it.

7
00:00:25,400 --> 00:00:29,334
And add the superbill, with the service and diagnosis codes.

8
00:00:32,267 --> 00:00:35,210
This module covers the last, and most important,

9
00:00:35,260 --> 00:00:40,948
step of the monthly process for every patient: submitting the encounter for billing.

10
00:00:41,400 --> 00:00:45,329
Practice Fusion is the platform used to bill the insurance.

11
00:00:45,600 --> 00:00:49,748
So every step here must be done with care, to avoid any issues.

12
00:00:50,267 --> 00:00:54,243
Log in to Practice Fusion with your own username and password.

13
00:00:54,293 --> 00:00:56,366
Each agent has their own.

14
00:01:02,433 --> 00:01:06,168
Practice Fusion is divided into tabs, on the left.

15
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:12,449
Open Charts.

16
00:01:12,700 --> 00:01:16,150
To find a patient, use the search bar at the top.

17
00:01:16,400 --> 00:01:19,463
You can search by name, or by date of birth.

18
00:01:19,933 --> 00:01:21,327
Search by date of birth.

19
00:01:21,377 --> 00:01:24,937
It avoids opening a different patient who has the same name,

20
00:01:24,987 --> 00:01:27,241
but a different date of birth.

21
00:01:29,367 --> 00:01:33,171
Type two digits for the month, two for the day, and then the year.

22
00:01:36,367 --> 00:01:37,634
Then search.

23
00:01:39,733 --> 00:01:43,244
The results show every patient with that exact date of birth.

24
00:01:43,294 --> 00:01:46,020
Open the one that matches your patient.

25
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:50,569
Here, it's this one.

26
00:01:56,633 --> 00:01:58,232
The patient's chart opens.

27
00:01:58,282 --> 00:02:02,282
Encounters, on the right, lists the previous encounters.

28
00:02:02,533 --> 00:02:04,300
There's one encounter each month,

29
00:02:04,350 --> 00:02:08,212
since each patient in the program is followed up once a month.

30
00:02:08,467 --> 00:02:13,511
Each one is a PCM Monthly Care Plan encounter, about a month apart.

31
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:22,301
So create a new encounter for this month.

32
00:02:22,351 --> 00:02:24,981
Click the arrow next to New encounter.

33
00:02:28,367 --> 00:02:30,493
It lists the encounter types.

34
00:02:30,543 --> 00:02:34,520
Ours is always the same: PCM Monthly Care Plan.

35
00:02:34,800 --> 00:02:38,986
Select it, and the system creates the new encounter for this patient.

36
00:02:41,133 --> 00:02:43,941
The new encounter opens, dated today.

37
00:02:48,867 --> 00:02:52,956
First, set the encounter's general information: who saw the patient,

38
00:02:53,006 --> 00:02:54,490
and the facility.

39
00:02:55,167 --> 00:02:57,226
Seen by is the patient's provider.

40
00:02:57,276 --> 00:02:59,832
It's in the task information you received,

41
00:02:59,882 --> 00:03:03,621
with the patient's name, date of birth, and facility.

42
00:03:07,667 --> 00:03:09,999
Here, it's Joseph Fagbohun.

43
00:03:14,067 --> 00:03:16,703
Next, the facility where the patient lives.

44
00:03:16,753 --> 00:03:18,640
Open the Facility list.

45
00:03:19,933 --> 00:03:24,234
It's a long list, so use Control F to find the facility's name.

46
00:03:24,933 --> 00:03:27,317
Here, it's Haven of Farmer City.

47
00:03:27,567 --> 00:03:32,041
Now the general information is correct: the provider assigned to the patient,

48
00:03:32,091 --> 00:03:34,127
and the patient's facility.

49
00:03:41,967 --> 00:03:44,093
Now, scroll down to the note.

50
00:03:44,533 --> 00:03:47,480
Next is the PCM Monthly Care Plan section.

51
00:03:47,530 --> 00:03:51,190
Every encounter needs the same template here.

52
00:03:54,000 --> 00:03:55,940
It's in the CCM Clinical Tool,

53
00:03:55,990 --> 00:04:00,752
on the Templates page: under Practice Fusion, the care plan note.

54
00:04:04,000 --> 00:04:06,483
Copy it, and paste it into the section.

55
00:04:07,600 --> 00:04:11,775
It reads: See attached ThoroughCare care plan dated, then a date,

56
00:04:11,825 --> 00:04:16,565
for time spent, care coordination activities, and patient consent.

57
00:04:16,867 --> 00:04:19,497
The date is the exact date of the encounter.

58
00:04:19,547 --> 00:04:22,067
Take it from the encounter itself.

59
00:04:26,100 --> 00:04:29,778
Next: Time spent on care coordination: 60 minutes.

60
00:04:29,828 --> 00:04:33,857
Each encounter is billed for exactly 60 minutes.

61
00:04:36,267 --> 00:04:41,022
Then: See ThoroughCare plan dated, with the same date, for full details.

62
00:04:41,300 --> 00:04:45,283
That's today's date, but take it from the encounter, to be sure.

63
00:04:49,333 --> 00:04:52,290
Next, upload the care plan file itself.

64
00:04:54,333 --> 00:04:55,556
In the earlier steps,

65
00:04:55,606 --> 00:04:59,857
you formulated the problem note from the patient's PointClickCare data,

66
00:04:59,907 --> 00:05:02,583
and documented the care plan in ThoroughCare,

67
00:05:02,633 --> 00:05:05,385
following the documentation standards.

68
00:05:05,667 --> 00:05:09,111
Then you exported the care plan file from ThoroughCare.

69
00:05:09,161 --> 00:05:11,708
Now, attach it to this encounter.

70
00:05:16,100 --> 00:05:19,326
Under Documents attached to encounter, click Add.

71
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:23,786
This window lists files already uploaded for earlier encounters.

72
00:05:23,836 --> 00:05:25,785
Don't select any of them.

73
00:05:30,633 --> 00:05:31,952
Click Upload.

74
00:05:32,233 --> 00:05:36,485
Choose the patient's care plan file from your computer, and open it.

75
00:05:38,067 --> 00:05:40,455
Select the file, and click Open.

76
00:05:46,900 --> 00:05:49,560
The file is now attached to the encounter.

77
00:05:52,833 --> 00:05:55,503
Click the file name to edit its details.

78
00:05:57,133 --> 00:05:58,322
First, the provider.

79
00:05:58,372 --> 00:06:02,663
It's set to Marawan Khaled, who isn't this patient's provider.

80
00:06:05,067 --> 00:06:08,859
Change it to the patient's provider: Joseph Fagbohun.

81
00:06:10,500 --> 00:06:14,347
Then check the file itself, so nothing is wrong or missing.

82
00:06:17,967 --> 00:06:21,481
The patient's name must match the name in the profile.

83
00:06:21,733 --> 00:06:26,450
Note: the file attached in this recording is a sample from another patient,

84
00:06:26,500 --> 00:06:27,594
and another month.

85
00:06:27,644 --> 00:06:32,289
In real work, attach only this month's care plan for this patient.

86
00:06:32,567 --> 00:06:36,175
The provider must match the one in the encounter details.

87
00:06:39,633 --> 00:06:42,432
The problem list shows the SNF care plan,

88
00:06:42,482 --> 00:06:46,475
and the program: PCM, or Principal Care Management.

89
00:06:48,867 --> 00:06:51,557
And the month's problem note is in the file.

90
00:06:54,933 --> 00:06:57,645
Last, the time log, near the end of the file.

91
00:06:57,695 --> 00:06:59,556
It's vital for billing.

92
00:07:01,133 --> 00:07:04,047
Scroll down to the last pages of the file.

93
00:07:08,867 --> 00:07:13,681
The category must be Monthly Clinical Review, the category always used.

94
00:07:14,300 --> 00:07:18,513
The time must be logged as performed by the provider himself.

95
00:07:21,633 --> 00:07:24,712
And the time must be exactly 60 minutes.

96
00:07:25,733 --> 00:07:30,637
Once the file is checked, and the provider is updated, save the details.

97
00:07:33,033 --> 00:07:34,444
Next, add the superbill.

98
00:07:34,494 --> 00:07:37,866
Under Superbill, click Add, to create a new one.

99
00:07:39,167 --> 00:07:43,420
Only two services are used, each with an exact service code.

100
00:07:45,000 --> 00:07:48,589
Find them under Frequently used codes, or search for them.

101
00:07:51,000 --> 00:07:53,173
Type the code in the search box.

102
00:07:56,400 --> 00:07:59,251
The first code is 99426.

103
00:07:59,533 --> 00:08:04,535
It's for principal care management services, for a single high-risk disease.

104
00:08:09,333 --> 00:08:12,302
Then click Add service, for a second service.

105
00:08:13,867 --> 00:08:17,597
Its code is the next one: 99427.

106
00:08:20,833 --> 00:08:26,886
These two codes, 99426 and 99427, are used to bill every encounter,

107
00:08:26,936 --> 00:08:30,210
with one service for each code.

108
00:08:30,833 --> 00:08:32,154
Under each service,

109
00:08:32,204 --> 00:08:37,920
add the exact diagnosis code: the ICD-10 code of the patient's condition.

110
00:08:39,500 --> 00:08:44,905
For this patient, it's I50.32, chronic diastolic heart failure.

111
00:08:45,167 --> 00:08:46,811
Do the same for Service 2.

112
00:08:46,861 --> 00:08:51,026
Now each service has a billing code and a diagnosis code.

113
00:08:53,433 --> 00:08:56,991
For a follow-up patient, you're done with the services.

114
00:08:58,300 --> 00:09:02,241
But this patient is a scratch patient: he was just enrolled.

115
00:09:05,467 --> 00:09:09,994
Scroll down to Service 2, the 99427 service.

116
00:09:15,667 --> 00:09:19,115
For a scratch patient, add a third service,

117
00:09:19,165 --> 00:09:22,288
with the same code as Service 2, 99427.

118
00:09:22,338 --> 00:09:25,148
Click Duplicate on Service 2.

119
00:09:25,400 --> 00:09:32,031
So a follow-up patient has two services: 99426 and 99427.

120
00:09:32,081 --> 00:09:38,626
A scratch patient has three: 99426, and 99427 twice.

121
00:09:43,333 --> 00:09:47,632
One last check: the service details, inside the superbill.

122
00:09:50,033 --> 00:09:53,369
Scroll down to Service details, and expand them.

123
00:09:54,933 --> 00:09:58,107
Make sure the provider and the facility are correct.

124
00:10:03,700 --> 00:10:04,932
Then save the superbill.

125
00:10:04,982 --> 00:10:07,569
You're officially done with the patient.

126
00:10:07,833 --> 00:10:10,181
A message confirms that it's saved.

127
00:10:14,600 --> 00:10:17,672
If the service details are wrong, click Edit.

128
00:10:20,367 --> 00:10:24,719
Then set the rendering provider, the billing provider, and the facility.

129
00:10:29,133 --> 00:10:30,392
To recap.

130
00:10:30,667 --> 00:10:32,844
Find the patient by date of birth,

131
00:10:32,894 --> 00:10:36,554
and create a new PCM Monthly Care Plan encounter.

132
00:10:36,833 --> 00:10:41,039
Set Seen by to the patient's provider, and the patient's facility.

133
00:10:41,300 --> 00:10:45,397
Add the care plan note, with the encounter date and 60 minutes.

134
00:10:45,667 --> 00:10:48,117
Upload the care plan file, set its provider,

135
00:10:48,167 --> 00:10:51,742
and check the name, the problem note, and the time log.

136
00:10:52,000 --> 00:10:59,185
Add a superbill with 99426 and 99427, each with the diagnosis code.

137
00:10:59,467 --> 00:11:04,028
For a scratch patient, add a third 99427 service.

138
00:11:04,300 --> 00:11:07,158
Then check the service details, and save.

139
00:11:09,633 --> 00:11:11,804
That's the end of Module 5.

140
00:11:12,067 --> 00:11:15,339
Next, in Module 6: additional concepts.
